---
import { principles } from "../../data/principles";
import { metric } from "../../data/measured";

const velocityPrecision = metric("fraud.velocity.pr").value.split(" / ")[0];
---

<ol class="grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border bg-border md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
  {principles.map((p, i) => (
    <li class="reveal flex flex-col bg-surface p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] text-accent-fg">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</p>
      <h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight">{p.title}</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 flex-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{p.body}</p>
      <a href={p.evidence.href} class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 self-start rounded-sm font-mono text-[11px] text-accent-fg hover:underline">
        <span class="text-muted">Evidence:</span> {p.evidence.label} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </li>
  ))}
  <li class="reveal flex flex-col justify-center bg-surface-2 p-6">
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      These show up in the details: a velocity rule published with its {velocityPrecision}
      precision and the sweep that fixes it, a Great Expectations stub labelled
      as a stub, a benchmark scorer fixed and re-measured once it was caught counting the query's own text.
    </p>
  </li>
</ol>
